==================================================================
DAY 60 - PART B: LAB
Inspect a CSI driver, then add RWX storage with NFS
Time: 90-120 minutes
==================================================================

kubectx kind-lab
mkdir -p ~/k8s-journey/week9/csi && cd $_


STEP 1: kind's provisioner is NOT a CSI driver
----------------------------------------------
k get csidriver                 # probably empty
k get sc standard -o jsonpath='{.provisioner}{"\n"}'   # rancher.io/local-path
The local-path provisioner is an "external provisioner" that creates
hostPath-style PVs; no CSI attach/mount steps.


STEP 2: Run an NFS server inside the cluster (lab only)
-------------------------------------------------------
Follow the csi-driver-nfs example (it provides a ready NFS server
manifest):
k create ns nfs
k apply -n nfs -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes-csi/csi-driver-nfs/master/deploy/example/nfs-provisioner/nfs-server.yaml
k get pods,svc -n nfs
(The example creates Service "nfs-server". If the namespace inside the
manifest differs, follow the manifest.)


STEP 3: Install csi-driver-nfs
------------------------------
helm repo add csi-driver-nfs https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes-csi/csi-driver-nfs/master/charts
helm repo update
helm install csi-driver-nfs csi-driver-nfs/csi-driver-nfs -n kube-system
k get pods -n kube-system -l app.kubernetes.io/instance=csi-driver-nfs -o wide

Inspect the pieces:
k get deploy -n kube-system | grep nfs        # controller
k get ds -n kube-system | grep nfs            # node plugin
k get pod -n kube-system -l app=csi-nfs-controller -o jsonpath='{.items[0].spec.containers[*].name}{"\n"}'
   -> csi-provisioner, csi-snapshotter?, liveness-probe, nfs ...
k get pod -n kube-system -l app=csi-nfs-node -o jsonpath='{.items[0].spec.containers[*].name}{"\n"}'
   -> liveness-probe, node-driver-registrar, nfs
k get csidriver nfs.csi.k8s.io -o yaml | grep -A6 spec
k get csinode -o yaml | grep -B2 -A4 nfs.csi.k8s.io


STEP 4: StorageClass and an RWX PVC
-----------------------------------
vi sc-nfs.yaml

apiVersion: storage.k8s.io/v1
kind: StorageClass
metadata:
  name: nfs-csi
provisioner: nfs.csi.k8s.io
parameters:
  server: nfs-server.nfs.svc.cluster.local
  share: /
reclaimPolicy: Delete
volumeBindingMode: Immediate
mountOptions:
- nfsvers=4.1

vi pvc-rwx.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: shared
spec:
  accessModes: ["ReadWriteMany"]
  storageClassName: nfs-csi
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: 1Gi

k apply -f sc-nfs.yaml -f pvc-rwx.yaml
k get pvc shared                # Bound immediately
k get pv -o yaml | grep -A5 "csi:"
k logs -n kube-system -l app=csi-nfs-controller -c csi-provisioner --tail=5


STEP 5: Many pods, many nodes, one volume
-----------------------------------------
vi deploy-rwx.yaml

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: writers
spec:
  replicas: 4
  selector:
    matchLabels: {app: writers}
  template:
    metadata:
      labels: {app: writers}
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: w
        image: busybox:1.36
        command: ["sh", "-c", "while true; do echo \"$(date +%T) $(hostname) on $NODE\" >> /shared/log.txt; sleep 3; done"]
        env:
        - name: NODE
          valueFrom:
            fieldRef: {fieldPath: spec.nodeName}
        volumeMounts:
        - name: s
          mountPath: /shared
      volumes:
      - name: s
        persistentVolumeClaim:
          claimName: shared

k apply -f deploy-rwx.yaml
k get pods -l app=writers -o wide       # spread over both workers
sleep 15
k exec deploy/writers -- tail -8 /shared/log.txt

All pods on all nodes write to the same file: ReadWriteMany.
Compare: Day 28 WordPress needed Recreate because its PVC was RWO.


STEP 6: See the mounts on a node
--------------------------------
NODE=$(k get pod -l app=writers -o jsonpath='{.items[0].spec.nodeName}')
docker exec $NODE sh -c "mount | grep nfs"
Find the global staging mount and the per-pod bind mounts.


STEP 7: Clean up and commit
---------------------------
k delete deploy writers ; k delete pvc shared ; k delete sc nfs-csi
helm uninstall csi-driver-nfs -n kube-system ; k delete ns nfs
cd ~/k8s-journey && git add . && git commit -m "day60: csi"
